# Kernel sources of the module: static analysis only. Style is the business of .clang-format, and
# the style checks clang-tidy offers are not the kernel's.
#
# Disabled on purpose, each with the site that made it necessary:
#
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.*
#       The C11 Annex K *_s functions it asks for do not exist in the kernel.
#
#   clang-analyzer-unix.Malloc
#       The policy is built, filled in and then published with rcu_replace_pointer() while the
#       pointer stays owned by the module (policy_apply()). A stored pointer is a leak to this
#       check, so it reports the live policy as leaked.
#
#   clang-analyzer-core.UndefinedBinaryOperatorResult
#       patch.c memcpy()s from a request struct an earlier function filled in; the analyzer cannot
#       follow it across the queue and calls the source garbage.
#
#   clang-analyzer-core.BitwiseShift
#       hash_line() shifts by 32 + shift, and the layout only ever produces shift <= 28 (nlines
#       starts at POLICY_MIN_LINES, which is 16, and doubles), which the analyzer cannot see.
#
# Everything else in clang-analyzer-* is on.
Checks: >-
  -*,clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-unix.Malloc,
  -clang-analyzer-core.UndefinedBinaryOperatorResult,
  -clang-analyzer-core.BitwiseShift
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/hma-uidfake/src/.*'
WarningsAsErrors: ''
